
1. Core philosophy of the system
Holistic, not analytic:
The simulation never “cuts” the world into isolated modules conceptually; it treats everything as a single evolving field of relations. Modules exist in code, but the ontology is unified.
State as a living field:
There is one global state object (or graph) that represents the entire universe of the simulation at a given time step.
Reversible time:
Every update rule is designed to be invertible, so you can step forward or backward without loss.
Encrypted evolution:
The mapping from state(t) → state({t+1}) is both:
Physically meaningful (e.g., field equations, constraints)
Cryptographically structured (e.g., permutations, key-based transforms) so that the evolution itself can be treated as an encryption/decryption process.

